== Dependencies ==

This plugin depends on the following components to be installed:


  - [http://trac-hacks.org/wiki/XmlRpcPlugin TracXMLRPC]  ,,Since version 
    ''' 1.0.0 ''',, . This package will be installed by default. If not found
    then nothing will work.

  - [http://hessianpy.sourceforge.net HessianPy]  ,,Since version 
    ''' 1.0.0 ''',, . This package will be installed by default and is required
    in order to access Trac API via
    [http://hessian.caucho.com/doc/hessian-1.0-spec.xtp Hessian RPC].

  - [http://wiki.github.com/jkp/soaplib-lxml soaplib]  ,,Since version 
    ''' 1.0.0 ''',, . This package will be installed by default and is required
    in order to access Trac API via
    [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SOAP_(protocol) SOAP RPC].
    Currently there are plans to add support for HTTP transport
    but [http://xmpp.org/extensions/xep-0072.html XMPP transport]
    may be available too in a near future.

  - [http://pypi.python.org/pypi/xmppxmlrpc xmppxmlrpc]  ,,Since version 
    ''' 1.0.0 ''',, . This package cannot be installed by default because the
    original distribution seems not to be ''easy_installable''.
    So you need to install it and configure it by hand.
    It is required in order to access Trac API via
    [http://xmpp.org/extensions/xep-0009.html Jabber-RPC].

== Installation ==

This plugin has been tested with 
[http://trac.edgewall.org/ Trac]  [http://trac.edgewall.org/wiki/0.11 0.11.1] .  You can see it in action [https://opensvn.csie.org/traccgi/swlcu here] . 

The first step to make it work is to [wiki:TracPlugins install this plugin] 
either for a particular environment or otherwise make it available to
all the environments:

{{{
$ easy_install /path/to/unpacked/TracRpcProtocols-x.y.z.zip
}}}

,, where ''x.y.z'' is the version of the plugin,,

... or alternately ...

{{{
$ easy_install TracRpcProtocols
}}}

In case of having internet connection and access to 
[http://pypi.python.org/pypi PyPI] or a simlar repository, both these 
methods '''should''' automatically retrieve the [#Dependencies external 
dependencies] from there.

== Configuration ==

In order to enable [wiki:/En/Devel/TracRpcProtocols TracRpcProtocols] plugin, 
the only thing to do is to add the following lines to [wiki:TracIni trac.ini].

{{{
[components]
tracrpcext.* = enabled
}}}

